    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0351" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383 J 41/37: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-27T14:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Department’s telegram number 23 January 24th 4 p.m. As reported in Embassy’s
                    despatch number 2798 January 21st,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d302-f1"/> local press
                    of 21st instant published interview with Acting Secretary of Foreign Affairs to
                    the effect that although he is not in possession of precise information of the
                    present status of the judicial investigation in the Jenkins case, nevertheless
                    he is of the opinion that all international difficulties growing out of the case
                    have terminated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
